<div class="panel-inner">
  <h2 class="panel-title">About Me</h2>

  <div class="about-layout">
    <div class="about-body">
      <p>
        I'm Ofer — a product and technology leader with hands-on experience managing and delivering
        national-scale geospatial data systems and products. I own the full lifecycle: requirements
        discovery, system architecture, cross-functional delivery, and adoption — coordinating engineering,
        GIS, and government stakeholders across multiple countries.
      </p>
      <p>
        My foundation is in structured data, metadata, and information architecture, with a track record
        of translating complex operational needs into scalable, data-driven products and measurable
        outcomes. Much of that analytical grounding comes from urban mobility research — my Master's
        thesis at Tel Aviv University analysed over one million shared e-scooter rides to quantify the
        effect of cycling infrastructure on rider behaviour, sharpening both my data science craft and my
        ability to turn findings into actionable recommendations.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm self-taught in applied AI and large language models, with hands-on experience building and
        experimenting with grounded, tool-calling agents on real projects — and I'm now growing this into
        a core product focus, bringing the same structured, requirements-driven approach to AI-enabled
        products.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the delivery side, I lead national-scale Spatial Data Infrastructure (SDI) programmes in
        Zanzibar and Ogun State, Nigeria — coordinating developers, government stakeholders, and technical
        teams across multiple time zones, and owning everything from requirements gathering and system
        architecture to delivery and knowledge transfer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Geospatial technology is the domain I know best, but the skills I lean on most — structured
        problem-solving, data-driven decision making, and getting diverse teams aligned around a goal —
        travel well beyond any single field.
      </p>
    </div>

